# Business Operations Manual
## Juniper Dermatology

*Prepared for external B2B partners, consultants, marketing agencies, and service providers.*

---

## 1. Company Overview

### 1.1 Business Name
Juniper Dermatology

### 1.2 Industry
Healthcare — Medical, Surgical, and Cosmetic Dermatology

### 1.3 Core Products or Services
Juniper Dermatology is a dermatology clinic. It provides medical skin care, surgical skin care, and cosmetic skin care for patients of all ages, including children.

### 1.4 Target Customers
Patients in Bend, Redmond, and the broader Central Oregon region who need skin care for medical, surgical, or cosmetic reasons. The clinic accepts new patients and serves the whole family, including children.

### 1.5 Value Proposition
Juniper Dermatology offers patient-centered, whole-person skin care guided by osteopathic medical philosophy. The clinic combines advanced treatments with a personal, compassionate approach. Same-week appointments are available. It is one of the few practices in the region offering non-surgical skin cancer treatment (GentleCure / image-guided superficial radiotherapy).

### 1.6 Business Model

**How the company makes money:**
Juniper Dermatology bills patients directly and through health insurance for medical and surgical dermatology services. Cosmetic services are typically out-of-pocket and paid by the patient.

**Pricing model:**
- Medical and surgical services: billed through health insurance (insurance-based revenue)
- Cosmetic services: fee-for-service, out-of-pocket
- Cosmetic procedure pricing is listed on the website
- A cosmetic consultation fee applies for cosmetic visits
- A cancellation and late-change policy is in place

**Revenue streams:**
- Medical dermatology visits (office consultations, diagnosis, prescription management)
- Surgical procedures (biopsies, removals, excisions, skin cancer treatment)
- Cosmetic procedures (laser, injectables, aesthetic treatments)
- Retail skincare product sales (SkinBetter Science, SkinCeuticals, EltaMD, Nutrafol)
- Financing is offered through Cherry for cosmetic procedures

---

## 2. Customer Segments

### 2.1 Ideal Customer Profile
Adults and families in Central Oregon who need dermatology care. This includes people who have a skin condition that needs diagnosis or treatment, people who want cosmetic skin improvements, and people who want routine skin cancer screening. The clinic also sees children.

### 2.2 Customer Industries
Not applicable — the customer is the individual patient, not a business.

### 2.3 Customer Size
Individual patients and families. No minimum or maximum. New patients are accepted.

### 2.4 Common Customer Problems
- Chronic skin conditions: acne, psoriasis, eczema, rosacea, hyperhidrosis (excessive sweating), melasma
- Skin growths: moles, lipomas, cysts, keloids, warts
- Skin cancer concerns: suspicious spots, skin screenings, diagnosis, and treatment
- Nail problems: fungal nail infections
- Cosmetic concerns: aging skin, sun damage, unwanted hair, uneven skin tone, fine lines, volume loss
- Hair loss
- Seeking non-surgical options for skin cancer treatment

### 2.5 Typical Customer Goals
- Get a diagnosis and treatment for a skin problem
- Have a skin cancer screening done
- Remove or treat skin growths
- Improve the appearance of their skin
- Manage a long-term skin condition with ongoing care

---

## 3. Product / Service Breakdown

### 3.1 Core Services

**Adult and Pediatric Medical Dermatology**
Diagnosis and treatment of skin, hair, and nail conditions for patients of all ages. Examples include acne, eczema, psoriasis, rosacea, melasma, rashes, nail fungus, hyperhidrosis, keloids, and skin cancer.

**Surgical / Procedural Dermatology**
In-office procedures including:
- Skin biopsies (to test suspicious spots)
- Mole removal
- Lipoma removal
- Excision of cysts and other growths
- Skin cancer treatment via GentleCure (image-guided superficial radiotherapy — non-surgical option for basal cell and squamous cell carcinomas)
- Coordination of Mohs surgery referrals for high-risk skin cancers (Mohs is not performed in-office; it is referred out to specialists)

**Skin Cancer Screening**
Full-body skin exams to check for early signs of melanoma, basal cell carcinoma, and squamous cell carcinoma. Offered as a standalone preventive service.

### 3.2 Optional Services

**Cosmetic Dermatology**
Non-medical, elective treatments to improve skin appearance. Services include:
- CO2 laser resurfacing (skin rejuvenation, texture improvement)
- Pulse dye laser / VBeam (targets redness, blood vessels; treats psoriasis plaques and eczema)
- Intense Pulsed Light (IPL) therapy (sun damage, pigmentation, redness)
- RF microneedling (skin tightening, collagen stimulation)
- Microneedling / SkinPen (skin texture and scarring)
- Dermaplaning (exfoliation)
- Chemical peels (VI Peel and others)
- Microdermabrasion
- Sculptra (injectable collagen stimulator for volume)
- Sclerotherapy (treatment of leg veins)
- PRP (platelet-rich plasma) injections
- Ultherapy (ultrasound skin tightening)
- Botox and neuromodulators (implied by cosmetic service offering)
- Nutrafol (dermatologist-recommended hair wellness supplement, sold in-office)

**Medical-Grade Skincare Products (retail)**
- SkinBetter Science
- SkinCeuticals
- EltaMD
- Nutrafol (hair supplement)

### 3.3 Product Features
- GentleCure is a notable differentiator — a non-surgical skin cancer treatment using image-guided superficial radiotherapy (SRT), available for basal cell and squamous cell carcinomas
- VBeam pulse dye laser is offered for both cosmetic and medical indications (psoriasis, eczema, rosacea, vascular lesions)
- CO2 laser treatments are scheduled for limited seasonal slots (primarily fall, when downtime is more acceptable post-sun season)
- Cherry financing is available for cosmetic procedures

### 3.4 Deliverables Clients Receive
- Diagnosis and treatment plan for skin conditions
- Prescriptions for topical or oral medications
- In-office procedure or treatment
- Skincare product recommendations
- Education on their condition and how to manage it at home
- Referrals to other specialists when needed (e.g., Mohs surgery)
- Follow-up care as needed

### 3.5 What Makes the Service Different
- Osteopathic philosophy: the physician treats the whole person, not just the skin condition
- Board-certified dermatologist (Dr. Pivik, DO, FAAD, FAOCD) leads care
- Non-surgical skin cancer treatment (GentleCure / SRT) is offered in-office — not widely available in the region
- Same-week appointments available — this is actively promoted
- Family-friendly: treats adults and children
- Two locations in Central Oregon (Bend and Redmond)

