## 10. Delivery System

### 10.1 Project Kickoff (Patient Visit)
Patient arrives at one of the two clinic locations. Check-in is completed at the front desk. Intake forms capture medical history and reason for visit.

### 10.2 Task Allocation
The provider (Dr. Pivik, Dacia Kailin PA-C, or Karrah) is assigned to the patient based on scheduling. Support staff handle intake, checkout, and billing.

### 10.3 Work Execution
- Medical visits: provider examines patient, diagnoses condition, discusses treatment options, prescribes medications or performs an in-office procedure
- Cosmetic visits: provider assesses the patient, recommends a treatment plan, performs or books the cosmetic procedure
- Procedures are performed in clinic using the appropriate equipment (laser, biopsy tools, SRT machine for GentleCure, etc.)
- CO2 laser procedures are limited to specific scheduled dates throughout the year

### 10.4 Quality Control
- Dr. Pivik is a board-certified dermatologist with FAAD and FAOCD credentials
- Osteopathic philosophy informs a whole-person approach to care
- Treatment protocols follow established dermatology standards
- For high-risk skin cancers, the clinic refers to Mohs surgery specialists rather than attempting complex cases in-office

### 10.5 Final Delivery
- Patient receives diagnosis, treatment, prescriptions, and/or procedure during the visit
- Aftercare instructions are provided
- Follow-up appointment is booked when appropriate
- Billing is processed through insurance or patient payment

