## 14. Summary of Business Operations

Juniper Dermatology is a two-location dermatology clinic in Central Oregon. It is owned and run by Dr. Karla Pivik, a board-certified dermatologist. The clinic serves patients of all ages — from children to adults — in Bend and Redmond, Oregon.

The clinic operates across three types of services. First, medical dermatology: diagnosing and treating skin conditions like acne, eczema, psoriasis, rosacea, and others. Second, surgical dermatology: in-office procedures like biopsies, mole removals, and skin cancer treatment. Third, cosmetic dermatology: elective aesthetic treatments like laser resurfacing, chemical peels, microneedling, and injectables.

A key differentiator is GentleCure, a non-surgical treatment for certain types of skin cancer. This is not widely available in the region and is actively promoted.

Patients find the clinic through Google search, Google Ads, the Google Business Profile, Instagram, and word of mouth. Same-week appointments are available, which is a competitive advantage in a specialty where wait times can be long.

The clinic currently has one physician (Dr. Pivik), one PA (Dacia Kailin), and one new provider being added (Karrah). Administrative staff handle scheduling, intake, and billing. Marketing is outsourced to external vendors.

Revenue comes from insurance-covered medical and surgical visits, fee-for-service cosmetic procedures, and retail skincare product sales. Cherry financing helps cosmetic patients pay for elective treatments.

The clinic has an active digital presence, with a WordPress website, Google Ads, Instagram, and a blog. A full website overhaul is in progress, being managed through a contract worker found on Upwork. Key areas of improvement include SEO, mobile performance, Google Ads tracking, content updates, and form management.

External B2B service providers can add the most value in the following areas: website and digital marketing management, Google Ads optimization, SEO, social media content, patient communication tools, medical photography, and practice technology (scheduling, EHR, communications).

